-- --acn-v2 only: determinant fields exposed by an OPTIONAL referenced component (Hdr) to its siblings, which read them
-- from the caller's AcnInsertedFieldRef (value 0 when hdr2 is absent). A stream with hdr2 absent and data2 present does
-- not hold the size of data2: the decoder fails with the error code of data2 (it decoded data2 with size 0). A
-- present-when on an exposed BOOLEAN field reads FALSE (x absent), the behaviour the encoder's check of an absent
-- producer requires. An ACN argument (pl2): the decoder of pl2.d fails, the field's reference says that the field is
-- not in the stream.
-- No directives: run by v4Tests/scripts/runWireTests.sh with 004_decode_test.c / 004_decode_test.adb (legacy rejects
-- fields of a referenced type used outside it).
WIRE DEFINITIONS AUTOMATIC TAGS ::= BEGIN
    Hdr ::= SEQUENCE { a INTEGER(0..255) }
    Payload ::= SEQUENCE { d OCTET STRING (SIZE(0..15)) }
    MyPDU ::= SEQUENCE {
        hdr2    Hdr OPTIONAL,
        data2   OCTET STRING (SIZE(0..15)) OPTIONAL,
        pl2     Payload OPTIONAL,
        x       INTEGER(0..255) OPTIONAL,
        tail    INTEGER(0..255)
    }
END
